experiments/k1116b/README.md:107:2. The `shift(2)` correction at weekly frequency is a conservative fix. Strictly, NFCI observed at Fri W-1 is released Wed W, so shift(1) at week-W-1 labeling means using NFCI[W-1] (labeled Fri W-1) during Mon-Tue W is technically lookahead of 3 days, while Wed-Fri W is fair use. Our fix trades away some signal to guarantee no leakage. The conservative variant (shift(2) for USEPU/WLEMU too) errs further on safety.
