experiments/k812/k812_us_taiwan_leadlag_results.json:431:  "conclusion": "★★★ Lead-lag strategies CAN beat BH. Best: Smooth tanh(SPY) (Sharpe 3.400 vs BH 0.908). Harvey threshold PASSED (4/4 strategies). Direction accuracy 64.1%. Beta(SPY→TW50)=0.43 (t=28.4). Cross-OOS: all strategies 5/5 wins. K502 found lead-lag untradable due to binary TX costs (58.5bp); this experiment shows VT-style smooth positioning resolves the TX problem. Smooth tanh(SPY) is regime-invariant (Sharpe 3.46/3.42 in low/high VIX). Key insight: smooth continuous weights >> binary switching for lead-lag signals. Sanity: lag verified (shift(1) correct), random baseline Sharpe 0.78 (z=19.6), same-day lookahead gives LOWER Sharpe (1.94 vs 3.78) confirming correct lag structure.",
