experiments/k950/k950_post_publish_codex_review.md:71:- L152 `shift(1)` correctly pushes the signal series forward by one trading day, so weight applied to day-t return = signal computed on day-(t-1). **Lookahead correctly prevented.**
experiments/k950/k950_post_publish_codex_review.md:72:- Article footer also explicitly states `signal.shift(1)` 防前瞻 — claim matches code.
experiments/k950/k950_post_publish_codex_review.md:77:- Transaction cost: code L167 uses `|Δw| * (cost_bps/10000) * 2`. Article says "10bps single-side". The 2× factor models one buy + one sell (equity leg + safe leg), each charged 10bps. A 0.5 weight swing → 0.5 × 0.001 × 2 = 10bps drag on portfolio = correct under "single-side" framing. **Not overstated.**
experiments/k950/k950_post_publish_codex_review.md:96:- ✓ `.shift(1)` present (see item 2)
experiments/k950/k950_post_publish_codex_review.md:109:| MEDIUM | Month-start VT comment says "applied to entire month's returns" but shift(1) means first trading day of month still uses prior month's regime. Not lookahead — just a 1-day implementation lag undisclosed in comments. | ✅ Fixed: comment clarified in review doc (no code change needed, behavior is conservative) |
experiments/k950/k950_post_publish_codex_review.md:113:**Lookahead**: ✅ PASS — `vix_monthly.loc[:date]` + `weights.shift(1)` confirmed no future leak.  
experiments/k950/k950_post_publish_codex_review.md:114:**Transaction costs**: ✅ PASS — `|Δw| * 2 * 10bps` correctly models two-leg round-trip.  
